          <declname>Channel</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>u32</type>
          <declname>Mask</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Clears interrupts. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Every bit set in Interrupt Status. Register indicates that a specific type of interrupt is occurring, and this function clears one or more interrupts by writing a bit mask to Interrupt Clear Register.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is a pointer to <ref refid="struct_x_csu_dma" kindref="compound">XCsuDma</ref> instance to be worked on. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">Channel</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Channel to operate on (XCSUDMA_SRC_CHANNEL or XCSUDMA_DST_CHANNEL). </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">Mask</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Bit mask of interrupts to clear, formed by OR&apos;ing XCSUDMA_IXR_* bits defined in <ref refid="xcsudma__hw_8h" kindref="compound">xcsudma_hw.h</ref>. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
